<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humphrey Gilbert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1539–<a href="/years/1583">1583</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sir Humphrey Gilbert, Gilbert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Humphrey Gilbert was an English soldier and explorer of the Elizabethan era. In 1583 he made a formal claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> for the English crown, but was lost at sea on the return voyage and left no settlers. His claim is conventionally treated as the founding moment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert.jpg" alt="Humphrey Gilbert" width="320" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Humphrey_Gilbert_Compton_Castle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
